                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/SensorsStore.js",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Not all systems support this, ideally we read from the API if this is supported \n\nFrom /redfish/v1/ \nhttps://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/ServiceRoot.v1_16_1.json\n\n\"ExpandQuery\": {\n\"ExpandAll\": true,\n\"Levels\": true,\n\"Links\": true,\n\"MaxLevels\": 6,\n\"NoLinks\": true\n},\n\nCan we read if \"ExpandQuery\"\"MaxLevels\" exists and if it is >0 and this to determine which branch to call."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/SensorsStore.js",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "+1.  Even if this becomes the default, it will be likely systems will disable it, or this webui gets loaded on non-openbmc systems.  We should do what the spec requires, and check the Expand/MaxLevels properties before using them, and fall back to normal iteration."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/SensorsStore.js",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
